# Architecture

The server is one process with three transports (HTTP, gRPC, and a Prometheus metrics endpoint), a shared handle registry called `AppState`, and a supervisor that owns the lifecycle of every task. Boot is a fixed, ordered sequence that fails closed. Once assembled, every transport and background worker runs under one supervisor that drains cooperatively on shutdown.

That one process bundles two Wyrd subsystems. The control plane stores and validates cards, derives their lineage, and enforces auth and policy. The Vala data plane records observations, the runs and traces your models and agents emit, and answers analytical queries against them. Vala's warehouse is **Bifrost**, an Apache Iceberg catalog whose table metadata lives in Postgres and whose data files live in object storage. That is why the [Database](/self-hosting/database/) roles include a Bifrost catalog role and a Vala recovery role. For the product-level split between these planes, see [Architecture](/concepts/architecture/) in Concepts.

